The Sparc was introduced in 1987.  And most places didn't get it
immediately: I can remember the old Motorola based systems being
present as late as 1990 where I worked at the time.

If 2.3e was released in 1987, it's very unlikely that they had
tested it on a Sparc (although you never know).  On the other
hand, the big difference between Sun OS 3 and Sun OS 4 was that
the latter ran on a Sparc.  They were both Berkley kernels, and
the C code was pretty compatible.

